# Off Centered Stack (locked mechanism)

**Say:** “use an Off Centered Stack”  
**Primitive:** [`LookbookOffCenteredStack`](../../src/components/direction-ef/lookbook/LookbookOffCenteredStack.tsx)  
**Shipped on:** Culture Archive (`/culture/archive`)

When asked for an Off Centered Stack, **always** implement (or reuse) this sticky mechanic. Do not invent a spaced flex column, horizontal swipe deck, or “lookalike” that only fades cards in.

## Required mechanism (do not regress)

| Requirement | Spec |
|-------------|------|
| Pin | Each plate wrapper is `position: sticky` with shared `top` (under crest, e.g. `4.5rem`) |
| Layer | Rising `z-index` so later prints stack **on top** of earlier ones while scrolling |
| Runway | Non-last plates need scroll padding (`paddingBottom` ~ `min(48vh, 22rem)`) so the next plate can climb over |
| Gap | **No** `flex gap-*` / large vertical gutters between plates — gap was the bug that made stacks “not stack” |
| Align | Off-center L/R with **edge inset** (`ml-2`–`md:ml-6` / matching `mr-*`) — not flush to the canvas edge |
| Cue | `Scroll` / `↓` — not Swipe, not ticker marquee |
| Motion | **Lead plate materializes on load** (opacity + y + slight scale/blur → settle, `LOOKBOOK_EASE`); later plates enter on scroll; honor `prefers-reduced-motion` |
| Links | Whole plate or `[ Read ]` may open external / route; 44px targets |

## Forbidden (causes the regression we already fixed)

- `flex flex-col gap-10` (or similar) as the plate list — creates large empty space; cards never overlap
- Document-flow only (`relative` plates, no sticky) with fade-in pretending to be a stack
- Cloning homepage [`Act2LookbookStack`](../../src/components/direction-ef/Act2LookbookStack.tsx) into interiors (home is frozen; different free-scroll / crest coupling)
- Horizontal snap “note deck” as a substitute for Off Centered Stack
- Infinite marquees, SaaS card chrome, rounded pills, Buy/Reserve/Book

## When to use

- Publication / issue series (Culture Archive and future magazine-style lists)
- Photo-led stacks where the user should **scroll to layer** prints, not swipe sideways

## When not to use

- FAQ / ruled indexes → faq-02 accordion
- Team portraits → team-03 alternating rows
- Frozen homepage lookbook close → `Act2LookbookStack` only

## Agent checklist

Before marking Off Centered Stack done:

1. Reuse `LookbookOffCenteredStack` — do not fork a new spaced list
2. Sticky wrappers present; list has **no** large flex gap between plates
3. On scroll, later plate visibly covers earlier (overlap) under shared sticky top
4. Labels match request (e.g. `// Archives`, `01 // Archive`)
5. Mobile 375: no horizontal page bleed; touch targets ≥ 44px
